    "summary": "Completed S1 initial-attempt design review with final production build, compiled normal stdio MCP/Unix IPC fake-CLI smoke, workflow-route matrix and focused regressions. One corrected native Claude Sonnet 5 run completed all nine chunks in 33m40s with retrievable feedback and an INCOMPLETE design verdict. This is useful execution evidence with explicit verification limits, not a clean design review or approval: test-coverage returned toy feedback after native schema errors and final consistency flagged that gap; exclude placeholder f1 from usable findings (7 MED/3 LOW, no HIGH). Other chunks inspected real linked designs/code but often used annotated refs instead of exact coverage tokens; host failed closed to incomplete. One earlier run failed status consistency after 11m10s; both checkpoints retained. Final prompt clarity corrections, native inactivity/late-output guards, replay and save-failure fences have deterministic tests and final compiled smoke coverage; no third hosted run was used to obtain a clean verdict. Full evidence and limitations: /tmp/design-review-s1-verification.json.",
